Linux System Audit (lsa-sysinfo) @VERSION@ - generic Linux x86_64 build
@UNDERLINE@

What this is: the same programs and files as @BUILT_FROM@, unpacked into a
plain directory so they can be used on other distributions. Built for plain
x86-64; the AVX2 / AVX-512 benchmark code is used only if the CPU has it.

Needs glibc @GLIBC@ or newer (check with: ldd --version). Older systems: use the
.deb/.rpm for your distribution from the release page instead.

Files (laid out like /usr):
  usr/bin/lsa-gui    GTK 3 window: the Cache & Memory Benchmark
  usr/bin/lsa        command line (lsa cachemem, lsa guide ITEM)
  usr/share/...      menu entries, icon, docs and the user guide (PDF + HTML)

Needed at run time
  - glibc @GLIBC@+, GTK 3 (libgtk-3-0 / gtk3), GLib, Cairo
  - hwdata (chipset names, read from /usr/share/hwdata)
  - optional: xdg-utils (opens the user guide), srs-sysinfo's srs-root cache
    (memory type / speed details), the ryzen_smu kernel driver (North Bridge
    Clock on Ryzen 7000 desktop CPUs)

Try it without installing
  ./usr/bin/lsa-gui
  ./usr/bin/lsa --version
  The user guide is found beside the program (usr/share/doc/lsa-sysinfo).

Install system-wide (recommended: /usr/local)
  sudo cp -r usr/bin usr/share /usr/local/
  sudo update-desktop-database /usr/local/share/applications 2>/dev/null || true
  sudo gtk-update-icon-cache -f /usr/local/share/icons/hicolor 2>/dev/null || true

  The "LSA User Guide (PDF)" menu entry opens /usr/share/doc/lsa-sysinfo/LSA-User-Guide.pdf.
  After installing to /usr/local, point it there:
    sudo sed -i 's|/usr/share/doc/|/usr/local/share/doc/|' /usr/local/share/applications/lsa-user-guide.desktop

Uninstall: remove the same files from /usr/local (see the file list in this tarball).

Arch Linux users: use the .pkg.tar.zst from the release or the AUR package lsa-sysinfo instead.
